% BAB/L/019, Science Museum Group Collection, document aa110001681.
% Cover 222/589 ("No 19", "31 July 1840"); the opened sheet 222/590 with the
% table and, at the right, "No & order of Varble Cards"; the back 222/591
% (222/592 is a second scan of the same back). Read from the zoom images at
% full resolution. See sources/notes/L019.md.
%
% DRAFT (.bab.draft, which build.rs does not read): the sheet needs two
% things the notation does not have, written here as they would be:
%   v6 0 a'     a number "given off & retained": the sheet writes a small 0
%              above and the letter below. The back: "This means give off &
%              retain; thus a is given off from a certain place which is
%              reduced to zero (denoted by the 0 above) & retained at the
%              same place (denoted by the position below) by means of its
%              Complement previously put out."
%   v22 C(a') 0   the complement laid in v22 and given back in the same
%              operation: the sheet writes "C'a" and a small 0 below it.
%   Cards n (v6 v22)(v2 0)...   the sheet's own list of variable cards for
%              each operation, "No & order of Varble Cards", in its notation
%              (first: the variable that gives off, 0 for the mill; second:
%              the variable that receives, 0 for the mill).
% A runnable version, with each retained read written as a read plus a
% transfer, is described in sources/notes/L019.md.
%
% Babbage writes the accents before the letter: 'a is a′, ''b is b″; and d
% is the round ∂. Here a', b'' and d.

Sheet BAB/L/019
No. 19
Date 31 Jul 1840          "31 July 1840"   % cover; the table's "31 July 1840" is written over another date
Title "Notation of the Reduction of the Four Equations"
Image 222/589 cover: the four equations aw + bx + cy + ∂z + e = 0 ('a, ''a, '''a …) "into" Bx + Cy + Dz + E = 0, 'Bx + 'Cy + 'Dz + 'E = 0, ''Bx + ''Cy + ''Dz + ''E = 0
Image 222/590 the table and the variable cards
Image 222/591 back: the meaning of the variable cards and of "give off & retain"

Letters a b c d e a' b' c' d' e' a'' b'' c'' d'' e'' a''' b''' c''' d''' e''' w x y z
% Store headings: v1-v5 a b c ∂ e under "aw + bx + cy + ∂z + e = 0"; v6-v10
% 'a … 'e; v11-v15 ''a … ''e; v16-v20 '''a … '''e. v21 "C.a … C.'''a",
% v22 "C.'a …", v23 unheaded (it holds C''a, C''b, …), v24 and v25
% "Product". A blank column after v5, v10, v15 and v20.
Store v1 = a, v2 = b, v3 = c, v4 = d, v5 = e, v6 = a', v7 = b', v8 = c', v9 = d', v10 = e', v11 = a'', v12 = b'', v13 = c'', v14 = d'', v15 = e'', v16 = a''', v17 = b''', v18 = c''', v19 = d''', v20 = e'''
Working v21 v22 v23 v24 v25

% Columns: "No of Opn"; braces, each grouping three operations and
% numbered 1 to 4 within each group of twelve, the twelve braced together;
% "Species of Opn"; "Resulting Quantity" (each subtraction written
% "'ab − a'b = B" and so on); "Ingress" and "Egress", empty throughout; the
% store.
Op 1   ×  | a'b            | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v2 0, v24 a'b |
Cards 1 (v6 v22)(v2 0)(v22 v6)(0 v24)
Op 2   ×  | ab'            | v1 0 a, v21 Ca 0, v7 0 b', v22 C(b') 0, v25 ab' |
Cards 2 (v1 v21)(v7 v22)(v21 v1)(v22 v7)(0 v25)
Op 3   −  | a'b-ab'        | v24 0, v25 0, v2 =B |
Cards 3 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v2)
Op 4   ×  | a'c            | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v3 0, v24 a'c |
Cards 4 (v6 v22)(v3 0)(v22 v6)(0 v24)
Op 5   ×  | ac'            | v1 0 a, v21 Ca 0, v8 0 c', v22 C(c') 0, v25 ac' |
Cards 5 (v1 v21)(v8 v22)(v21 v1)(v22 v8)(0 v25)
Op 6   −  | a'c-ac'        | v24 0, v25 0, v3 =C |
Cards 6 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v3)
Op 7   ×  | a'd            | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v4 0, v24 a'd |
Cards 7 (v6 v22)(v4 0)(v22 v6)(0 v24)
Op 8   ×  | ad'            | v1 0 a, v21 Ca 0, v9 0 d', v22 C(d') 0, v25 ad' |
Cards 8 (v1 v21)(v9 v22)(v21 v1)(v22 v9)(0 v25)
Op 9   −  | a'd-ad'        | v24 0, v25 0, v4 =D |
Cards 9 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v4)
Op 10  ×  | a'e            | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v5 0, v24 a'e |   % v24: the accent is run into the a, so that the product reads almost "be"; read a'e, as the mill column has it
Cards 10 (v6 v22)(v5 0)(v22 v6)(0 v24)
Op 11  ×  | ae'            | v1 0, v10 0 e', v22 C(e') 0, v25 ae' |   % no complement of a: a is not needed again; card (v1 0)
Cards 11 (v1 0)(v10 v22)(v22 v10)(0 v25)
Op 12  −  | a'e-ae'        | v24 0, v25 0, v5 =E |
Cards 12 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v5)
Op 13  ×  | a''b'          | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v7 0, v24 a''b' |   % a dashed line across the store above this row, and above 25: the groups of twelve
Cards 13 (v11 v23)(v7 0)(v23 v11)(0 v24)
Op 14  ×  | a'b''          | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v12 0 b'', v23 C(b'') 0, v25 a'b'' |
Cards 14 (v6 v22)(v12 v23)(v22 v6)(v23 v12)(0 v25)
Op 15  −  | a''b'-a'b''    | v24 0, v25 0, v7 =B' |
Cards 15 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v7)
Op 16  ×  | a''c'          | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v8 0, v24 a''c' |
Cards 16 (v11 v23)(v8 0)(v23 v11)(0 v24)
Op 17  ×  | a'c''          | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v13 0 c'', v23 C(c'') 0, v25 a'c'' |
Cards 17 (v6 v22)(v13 v23)(v22 v6)(v23 v13)(0 v25)
Op 18  −  | a''c'-a'c''    | v24 0, v25 0, v8 =C' |
Cards 18 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v8)
Op 19  ×  | a''d'          | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v9 0, v24 a''d' |
Cards 19 (v11 v23)(v9 0)(v23 v11)(0 v24)
Op 20  ×  | a'd''          | v6 0 a', v22 C(a') 0, v14 0 d'', v23 C(d'') 0, v25 a'd'' |
Cards 20 (v6 v22)(v14 v23)(v22 v6)(v23 v14)(0 v25)
Op 21  −  | a''d'-a'd''    | v24 0, v25 0, v9 =D' |
Cards 21 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v9)
Op 22  ×  | a''e'          | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v10 0, v24 a''e' |
Cards 22 (v11 v23)(v10 0)(v23 v11)(0 v24)
Op 23  ×  | a'e''          | v6 0, v15 0 e'', v23 C(e'') 0, v25 a'e'' |   % no complement of a': not needed again; card (v6 0)
Cards 23 (v6 0)(v15 v23)(v23 v15)(0 v25)
Op 24  −  | a''e'-a'e''    | v24 0, v25 0, v10 =E' |
Cards 24 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v10)
Op 25  ×  | a'''b''        | v16 0 a''', v21 C(a''') 0, v12 0, v24 a'''b'' |
Cards 25 (v16 v21)(v12 0)(v21 v16)(0 v24)
Op 26  ×  | a''b'''        | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v17 0, v25 a''b''' |
Cards 26 (v11 v23)(v17 0)(v23 v11)(0 v25)
Op 27  −  | a'''b''-a''b''' | v24 0, v25 0, v12 =B'' |
Cards 27 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v12)
Op 28  ×  | a'''c''        | v16 0 a''', v21 C(a''') 0, v13 0, v24 a'''c'' |
Cards 28 (v16 v21)(v13 0)(v21 v16)(0 v24)
Op 29  ×  | a''c'''        | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v18 0, v25 a''c''' |
Cards 29 (v11 v23)(v18 0)(v23 v11)(0 v25)
Op 30  −  | a'''c''-a''c''' | v24 0, v25 0, v13 =C'' |
Cards 30 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v13)
Op 31  ×  | a'''d''        | v16 0 a''', v21 C(a''') 0, v14 0, v24 a'''d'' |
Cards 31 (v16 v21)(v14 0)(v21 v16)(0 v24)
Op 32  ×  | a''d'''        | v11 0 a'', v23 C(a'') 0, v19 0, v25 a''d''' |
Cards 32 (v11 v23)(v19 0)(v23 v11)(0 v25)
Op 33  −  | a'''d''-a''d''' | v24 0, v25 0, v14 =D'' |
Cards 33 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v14)
Op 34  ×  | a'''e''        | v16 0, v15 0, v24 a'''e'' |   % the last pair retains nothing: cards (v16 0), (v11 0)
Cards 34 (v16 0)(v15 0)(0 v24)
Op 35  ×  | a''e'''        | v11 0, v20 0, v25 a''e''' |
Cards 35 (v11 0)(v20 0)(0 v25)
Op 36  −  | a'''e''-a''e''' | v24 0, v25 0, v15 =E'' |
Cards 36 (v24 0)(v25 0)(0 v15)

% Each group of twelve makes one equation free of w from two of the four:
% B … E from the first and second; 'B … 'E from the second and third;
% ''B … ''E from the third and fourth: the cover's three equations.
Composition B x + C y + D z + E = a'(a w + b x + c y + d z + e) - a(a' w + b' x + c' y + d' z + e')
Composition B' x + C' y + D' z + E' = a''(a' w + b' x + c' y + d' z + e') - a'(a'' w + b'' x + c'' y + d'' z + e'')
Composition B'' x + C'' y + D'' z + E'' = a'''(a'' w + b'' x + c'' y + d'' z + e'') - a''(a''' w + b''' x + c''' y + d''' z + e''')

Unrun "right of each group of three cards, the number of cards and a running total: 4 5 3 = 12, 4 5 3 = 24, 4 5 3 = 36, 4 4 3 = 47; 4 5 3 = 59, 4 5 3 = 71, 4 5 3 = 83, 4 4 3 = 94; 4 4 3 = 105, 4 4 3 = 116, 4 4 3 = 127, 3 3 3 = 136"
Remark "In the enumeration of Variable Cards as (v23 v7) the first variable as v23 is that which is given off the second as v7 is that which receive the number in v23. When the first variable place is occupied by zero it signifies that no Store Variable gives off but that the second variable receives from the Mill."
Remark "For the signification of [0 over a] and the like see back of No 18. This means give off & retain; thus a is given off from a certain place which is reduced to zero (denoted by the 0 above) & retained at the same place (denoted by the position below) by means of its Complement previously put out."
Unrun "back, pencil, after 'see back of No 18': 'what follows'; the '18' is written over other figures"
Unrun "cover, pencil, faint: 'A set of Variable Cards were made from this Notation'"
